/target

# Cargo.lock is tracked deliberately, even though this is a library crate:
# a downstream consumer resolves against its OWN lock file, not this one, so
# tracking it isn't about pinning what consumers get. It's tracked so CI
# builds reproducibly (the msrv job runs `cargo build --locked`), and so
# `cargo package`/`cargo publish` ship the exact dependency set that was
# actually tested rather than whatever `cargo update` would pick that day.
